---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ProjectDiagram from '../../components/ProjectDiagram.astro';
import ProjectHeader from '../../components/ProjectHeader.astro';
---

<Layout title="EKS Infrastructure with Terraform - Mark Lester Perez">
  <main class="project-page">
    <ProjectHeader />
    <h1>EKS Infrastructure with Terraform</h1>
    
    <section class="overview">
      <h2>Project Overview</h2>
      <p>
        A comprehensive Infrastructure as Code solution for deploying production-ready Amazon EKS clusters
        with advanced networking, security, and operational features using Terraform.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="technologies">
      <h2>Technologies Used</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>AWS EKS (Elastic Kubernetes Service)</li>
        <li>Terraform & Terragrunt</li>
        <li>AWS VPC & Networking</li>
        <li>AWS IAM for Service Accounts (IRSA)</li>
        <li>AWS Load Balancer Controller</li>
        <li>External DNS</li>
        <li>Cluster Autoscaler</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="implementation">
      <h2>Implementation Details</h2>
      
      <h3>Infrastructure Components</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Multi-AZ VPC with public and private subnets</li>
        <li>EKS cluster with managed node groups</li>
        <li>Auto-scaling configurations</li>
        <li>Security groups and network policies</li>
        <li>IAM roles and service accounts</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Security Features</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Network isolation with private subnets</li>
        <li>Pod security policies</li>
        <li>Encryption at rest for EBS volumes</li>
        <li>AWS KMS integration</li>
        <li>Security group rules for pod-to-pod communication</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Monitoring & Logging</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>AWS CloudWatch integration</li>
        <li>Container Insights</li>
        <li>Control plane logging</li>
        <li>Audit logging</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="architecture">
      <h2>Architecture Diagram</h2>
      <ProjectDiagram type="eks" />
    </section>

    <section class="architecture">
      <h2>Architecture Overview</h2>
      <p>
        The infrastructure follows AWS best practices and implements a highly available,
        secure, and scalable EKS cluster architecture:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Multi-AZ deployment for high availability</li>
        <li>Separate node groups for different workload types</li>
        <li>Private networking with NAT gateways</li>
        <li>Integration with AWS services via service accounts</li>
        <li>Automated backup and disaster recovery procedures</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .project-page {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 6rem 2rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 3rem;
    color: var(--heading);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  h2 {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  h3 {
    color: var(--heading);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem;
  }

  p {
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  ul {
    list-style-type: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  li {
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  li::before {
    content: "•";
    color: var(--accent);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
  }
</style>